    "summary": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud declared that Somalia's security forces are ready to take over the nation's security, marking a transition as foreign troops conclude their mission, during a ceremony in Galmudug.",
    "content": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud stated on Sunday that Somalia has reached a stage where its national army can handle security independently, making the continued presence of foreign forces increasingly unnecessary. He made these remarks during an event in Galmudug marking the completion of training for newly recruited Somali National Army soldiers.\n\nThe ceremony highlighted the government's broader strategy to strengthen the country's capacity to secure itself. The trained forces are expected to play a key role in areas where security responsibilities are being transferred from international troops to Somali hands, particularly in regions previously supported by the African Union Transition Mission in Somalia (ATMIS) and its successor, the African Union Support and Stabilization Mission in Somalia (AUSSOM).\n\nPresident Mohamud's comments come at a time when the Somali government has been gradually assuming more control over security operations in preparation for the eventual exit of foreign forces. The transition has been carefully planned to avoid creating a security vacuum, with Somali forces receiving training and logistical support from international partners to handle new responsibilities.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this transition carries significant implications. Many diaspora members have supported security reforms through remittances and investment in local institutions. A successful handover could enhance stability, potentially encouraging more investment and return of skilled professionals. However, challenges remain, including the need for careful integration of regional forces and sustained funding for the national army.\n\nThis development signals a significant phase in Somalia's path toward self-reliance, with the government emphasizing its commitment to maintaining peace without prolonged reliance on external military support. The coming months will be crucial in determining how effectively Somali forces manage security, particularly in areas where al-Shabaab remains active.",
